    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on exploiting favorable matchups against struggling arms, headlined by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Kyle Tucker** (71.27). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is our premier play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Ethan Pecko (5.95 xERA) and a massive 19% boost from the SP skill profile, compounded by an optimal batting order spot. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** remains a high-floor anchor; despite the middle-of-the-pack xERA of Bryce Elder, **Kyle Tucker**\u2019s elite base projections and consistent power profile keep him firmly in the \"Strong\" category. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.56) also earns a premium start, as his ability to handle Seth Lugo despite the dynamic platoon disadvantage is bolstered by a strong #2 hole projection.\n\nConversely, we face significant headwinds from elite arm talent, specifically when navigating matchups against deGrom, Glasnow, and Skenes. **Sam Antonacci** (46.72) draws the toughest assignment of the day against deGrom, though his leadoff status provides enough volume to justify the start. **Jackson Merrill** (49.46) faces a similar cold reality against Paul Skenes, and while his 13% platoon edge keeps him viable, he remains a candidate to watch for early removal if Skenes dominates. The bench decision for **Miguel Vargas** (39.59) was the most difficult; despite a strong xwOBA of .371, his projected score dipped below the 40-point floor due to the severe SP skill penalty imposed by facing deGrom, ultimately favoring the higher-ceiling outcomes of **Liam Hicks** (55.39) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (52.66).\n\nWe must exercise caution regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board, particularly for **Drake Baldwin** (43.58), whose utility is tethered to the assumption he occupies the #5 spot against the high-velocity threat of Tyler Glasnow. While **Nasim Nunez** (48.34) and **Coby Mayo** (47.55) are active, their proximity to our 40-point \"Below Floor\" threshold makes them strictly situational starts. Ensure that **Jordan Westburg** and **Andy Pages** remain safely on the IL; as the lead analyst, I am monitoring for any late-breaking weather patterns, but as of now, the primary risk remains the high concentration of elite SPs facing our mid-order bats.",
